": "matrix-condition", "usage_source": {"after": " &", "before": "& ", "environments": ["equation", "matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "matrix-if", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 242, "start": 240}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0003", "source": "if"}, {"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0004", "MATHSEG_0005"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 109576, "start": 109548}, "command_hash": "sha256:8f2fbc9cdb5dca19d455ea36e94cd65e218440205d12683f2c83c95aab0c0020", "container_byte_span": {"end": 109612, "start": 109294}, "container_hash": "sha256:bbc53d3e79e95011731e2ebdb228e6ca785f9c1c2837580efd1bfc38a2552210"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "etale-cohomology-section-kummer", "owner_tag": "03PK", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:29d7a759bdc4d4411eb3aeccfe7fcce5603644085ae4365b37f9ec839e6a1ee7", "source_label": "etale-cohomology-section-kummer", "usage": "etale-scheme-diagrams", "usage_source": {"after": "\n\\end{matrix}", "before": "\\varphi ", "environments": ["equation", "matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "etale-cohomology-c526a1e5e972", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 281, "start": 260}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0004", "source": " isomorphism of pairs"}], "source": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-isomorphisms-pairs}\n\\mathit{Isom}_S((\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha), (\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha'))\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\emptyset & \\text{if} & \\text{they are not isomorphic} \\\\\nH^0(S, \\mu_{n, S})\\cdot \\varphi & \\text{if} &\n\\varphi \\text{ isomorphism of pairs}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right.\n\\end{equation}", "source_byte_span": {"end": 1717, "start": 1399}, "source_hash": "sha256:bbc53d3e79e95011731e2ebdb228e6ca785f9c1c2837580efd1bfc38a2552210"}], "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PK", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-isomorphisms-pairs}\n\\mathit{Isom}_S((\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha), (\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha'))\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\emptyset & \\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "} & \\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "} \\\\\nH^0(S, \\mu_{n, S})\\cdot \\varphi & \\text{", "MATHSEG_0004": "} &\n\\varphi \\text{", "MATHSEG_0005": "}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right.\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n0 \\ar[r] &\nH_{fppf}^0(S, \\mu_{n, S}) \\ar[r] &\n\\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{O}_S^*) \\ar[r]^{(\\cdot)^n} &\n\\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{O}_S^*) \\ar@(rd, ul)[rdllllr]\n\\\\\n& H_{fppf}^1(S, \\mu_{n, S}) \\ar[r] &\n\\Pic(S) \\ar[r]^{(\\cdot)^n} &\n\\Pic(S) \\ar@(rd, ul)[rdllllr] \\\\\n& H_{fppf}^2(S, \\mu_{n, S}) \\ar[r] &\n\\ldots\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$n$", "MATH_0004": "$n \\in \\mathbf{N}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mu_n$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$\\alpha : \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n} \\to \\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0011": "$n$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha')$", "MATH_0014": "$\\varphi : (\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha) \\to (\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha')$", "MATH_0015": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{L} \\to \\mathcal{L}'$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n} \\ar[d]_{\\varphi^{\\otimes n}} \\ar[r]_\\alpha &\n\\mathcal{O}_S \\ar[d]^1 \\\\\n(\\mathcal{L}')^{\\otimes n} \\ar[r]^{\\alpha'} &\n\\mathcal{O}_S \\\\\n}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$(\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0018": "$(\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha')$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n(\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha) \\otimes (\\mathcal{L}', \\alpha')\n=\n(\\mathcal{L} \\otimes \\mathcal{L}', \\alpha \\otimes \\alpha')\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$(\\mathcal{O}_S, 1)$", "MATH_0021": "$$\n(\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha)^{-1} = (\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes -1}, \\alpha^{\\otimes -1}).\n$$", "MATH_0022": "$$\n(\\mathcal{L}, \\alpha)^{\\otimes n}\n=\n(\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}, \\alpha^{\\otimes n})\n\\xrightarrow{\\alpha}\n(\\mathcal{O}_S, 1)\n$$", "MATH_0023": "$n$", "MATH_0024": "$n$", "MATH_0025": "$\\Pic(S)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-picard-group}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-kummer-sequence-syntomic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:efbbdce30376027e2a03de31d2cd5b8c9eff7ddd09d143f7e02b7cd2c29464de", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:845bf21b0adeadd98323db0f35b9373bc3bb408907624f8611be0845ca6e5e9f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8229ac2ced3a5697078c465acc42858b0ee20d103062afd082669285f16ce9a7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBy\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nand\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand general properties of cohomology we obtain\nthe long exact cohomology sequence\n<MATH_0001>\nfor any scheme <MATH_0002> and any integer <MATH_0003>. Of course there is a similar sequence\nwith syntomic cohomology.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0004> and let <MATH_0005> be any scheme.\nThere is another more direct way to describe the first cohomology group with\nvalues in <MATH_0006>. Consider pairs\n<MATH_0007> where <MATH_0008> is an invertible sheaf on <MATH_0009>\nand <MATH_0010> is a trivialization\nof the <MATH_0011>th tensor power of <MATH_0012>.\nLet <MATH_0013> be a second such pair.\nAn isomorphism <MATH_0014>\nis an isomorphism <MATH_0015> of invertible\nsheaves such that the diagram\n<MATH_0016>\ncommutes. Thus we have\n<MATHSEG_0001>if<MATHSEG_0002>they are not isomorphic<MATHSEG_0003>if<MATHSEG_0004> isomorphism of pairs<MATHSEG_0005>\nMoreover, given two pairs <MATH_0017>, <MATH_0018>\nthe tensor product\n<MATH_0019>\nis another pair. The pair <MATH_0020> is an identity for this\ntensor product operation, and an inverse is given by\n<MATH_0021>\nHence the collection of isomorphism classes of pairs forms an abelian group.\nNote that\n<MATH_0022>\nis an isomorphism\nhence every element of this group has order dividing <MATH_0023>. We warn the reader\nthat this group is in general <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> the <MATH_0024>-torsion in <MATH_0025>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e270275749c8a09513be0f0e638442825639852192be8639707829398edb219", "unit_id": "tag:03PK:prose-0003"}
